Z||000005||Bazooka||06-23-2001||10:36 AM||||Flyguy, <BR>    I got my wingstands from 'Fiero Conversions' in Hamilton, Ontario, Can. It took abaout 3 weeks to get em, and they were sent from Focoa in California. The price was right for $105 including shipping. They are well designed as they have a sheet metal liner inside to prevent distortion and cracking. They don't include fasteners other than phillips head screws, but 'Ardell distributors' had the proper stock type for the 7"+ Wing. Best thing about em is they look appropriate to the styling of the Fiero GT and rear visibility is improved greatly. <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html</A> <BR>***********************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Flyguy:<BR><B>Does anybody know where i can get wing risers to raise it 7-10 inches<P>Thnx chris</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
